}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Boards+of+Canada+All+Reason+Departs", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Boards+of+Canada+All+Reason+Departs&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2026 Warp Records"]}, {"t": null, "time": "--:--:--", "artist": "ZumbiCore & DJ Synchro", "title": "A Void Como Seu Pai", "conf": "low", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=ZumbiCore+%26+DJ+Synchro+A+Void+Como+Seu+Pai", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=ZumbiCore+%26+DJ+Synchro+A+Void+Como+Seu+Pai", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=ZumbiCore+%26+DJ+Synchro+A+Void+Como+Seu+Pai", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/ZumbiCore+%26+DJ+Synchro+A+Void+Como+Seu+Pai", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=ZumbiCore+%26+DJ+Synchro+A+Void+Como+Seu+Pai", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/ZumbiCore+%26+DJ+Synchro+A+Void+Como+Seu+Pai", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=ZumbiCore+%26+DJ+Synchro+A+Void+Como+Seu+Pai&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“That was A Void Como Seu Pai by ZumbiCore and DJ Synchro, super fun track from Brazil”", "mentioned by the presenter but we couldn't work out when it played"]}], "counts": {"high": 13, "mid": 9, "low": 7}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:09:52", "end": "00:12:05", "text": "That is Waylay by Alsakuma Beats that you just heard and welcome to another episode of a Tuesday morning. I'm August. It's so nice to meet you. Thank you Sabine for an incredible three hours up for it. It's always one of my favorite shows to tune into first thing in the morning. and thank you zara afold for having been in this show for a couple of years um she's gonna be on new show so stay tuned for that but for now i will have you covered for this week and i'm super happy to be continue doing what sabine has been doing for the past three hours which is playing you awesome music and i'm grateful to be continuing that tradition from the aboriginal people of the land on which we are broadcasting on today in redfern at the station it's always was and always will be aboriginal land i have for you some incredible music for the next two hours until 12 p.m we have tracks from all i'm with the week from um saul williams and again amazing sydney music as always uh playing you 50 percent of australian music if not more here we're an independent station and we're just real people giving you the music that you deserve so support us um and without further ado the next track is from an independent artist here in sydney um the track is called you spoke to my march by and key does and lash monitor it's released independently of course and it's very diy sound um which i always love um and i feel you can hear the diy scene has been having kind of a resurgence here in sydney and everywhere which is so incredible to see and yeah text in at 04351239405 you're on fbi radio 94.5 m and this is nikita's and lash monitor you spoke to my march"}, {"start": "00:12:37", "end": "00:13:25", "text": "FBi Radio 94.5 Sydney with Zara Upfold. It's actually a nasty speech on my mind Little bit of me I'm fucking up back in a car while I'm puffing a car Next me, yeah she miss me I'm gonna skate, yeah, I'm hopping on a skate beat That girl, yeah, she can actually love me Yeah, but she just wanna fuck me I'm gonna suck on"}, {"start": "00:21:49", "end": "00:22:56", "text": "That was Crouch Rock by Kitty of the Valley. Just some super fun, punky guitar sounds. Kitty of the Valley is an independent band here from Eora, Sydney. They are a female-fronted art rock, punk rock band, which we love to see. um and i have even more australian music coming up for you the next track is called kings is a bit of a vibe switch from the track that i just played you from kitty valley um kiss it's an independent solo artist in halbert and i just got off his first australian tour so without further do this is the track called kings by kiss featuring even ooze in fbi radio this is tuesday morning with august and also language warning for you in this one"}, {"start": "00:36:56", "end": "00:38:14", "text": "That was, believe me, in parentheses, dust by Shearling. Shearling is an experimental rock band from California. I hope you guys enjoy the little rock sound we have there. And coming up, we're going to pick it up with Chil Cheney, an artist, an independent artist here from Sydney. um it's their latest single cool breeze and it's a really fun hip-hop sound um chill chenny is a kind of like full band project of uh rapper lance chenny it's evolved from a really raw solo act into this full live band with really fun hip-hop slash rock experimental energy so hopefully you guys enjoy that and Chilochini is also on their Worlds Collide regional and remote tour. They will be playing at the Oxford Art Factory on the 19th of November so get your tickets and hopefully I'll see you there and for now I'll leave you to it with Kubris, you're in FBI Radio, Tuesday morning with August"}, {"start": "00:54:30", "end": "00:55:36", "text": "The track you just heard was Slow Down by Kyla. Kyla is a super cool like EDM producer and artist based here and of course you're at Sydney and I'm gonna keep that going with Air Crash which is a new indie rock band that I saw at the Chippewa Hotel. So they are super cool. This is from their latest EP released in May called Head Cannon. And this track is called Cannon. And then after that, I will play you some more tracks from overseas. Have the new stuff from The Soundtrack Makes, which is one of my favorite artists right now. And of course, from all of the week, Leap Live by Saul Williams. So stay tuned. You're on Tuesday morning with FBI Radio 94.5. with august text in to where you feel where you're having for brunch um at zero four three five one two three nine four five and here is canon by air crash"}, {"start": "01:00:57", "end": "01:02:31", "text": "You just heard Electronic Eyes by The Sound Chalk Makes. It's one of my favorite artists that I just discovered recently. He's from Mumbai, India. Just really cool experimental EDM vibes. And coming up next, I will play you a track from All Up of the Week, Leap Live by Salt Williams. The track is called Not Everything For Sale. This album is really cool. It's multi-genera. Everything from hip-hop, drip-hop, pop. techno um kind of like deconstructed and mixed um it's really cool and unique and and talking about this album um salt williams says that the philosophy is the voice is the instrument and you can totally hear that and this track that i'm gonna play you our album of the week is basically um a record recently released that fbi has been loving and we've been having on rotation here at the station is selected by our amazing program music team it's all hand curated no ai no algorithms so if you want to keep really cool independent music discovered support us at fbi.fbi.radio slash support um you're in fbi again 94.5 fm with august here on tuesday morning and i'm gonna leave you to it with saul williams not everything for sale"}, {"start": "01:15:01", "end": "01:15:58", "text": "That was Four Blessings by Rainbow Chan. She is an independent solo artist here in Sydney. She's born in Hong Kong and you can totally hear that culture influence there. Such a fun track. It's from her latest album, The Bridal Lemon. and next up i have another really fun sound from scumlings scumling is again band from western australia and the track it's called stay with me t over s over m over g over o um it's super fun like the name and yeah i will end after that i will have more tracks from city and all over australia coming for you um so keep it locked you're on fbi radio 94.5 on tuesday morning with august and this is scumlings"}, {"start": "01:19:33", "end": "01:20:03", "text": "You're listening to Mornings. Seventh Day Brewery presents FOMO Saturdays, your home for live music on the northern beaches. Catch bands and DJs back-to-back all night long. Chill by the fire pit with an ice-cold beer or grab a slice of epic pizza by Saleh Pepe in the huge beer garden. Every Saturday at Seventh Day Brewery in Brookvale. For more info, head to Seventh Day Brewery's website and Instagram. Seventh Day Brewery, sponsors of FBi Radio."}, {"start": "01:23:27", "end": "01:23:43", "text": "We'll see you next time."}, {"start": "01:25:10", "end": "01:27:14", "text": "That was A Void Como Seu Pai by ZumbiCore and DJ Synchro, super fun track from Brazil. They are a really prominent underground Brazilian bass and funk artist, released independently, of course. And they're known for their kind of internet core, unique visual styling and presence. and very genre bounding as you've just heard um the next one i'm gonna play you it's may or may not be the best song titles i've heard in a while it's called this song may or not be about an alt-right influencer by portraits of tracy i got excited and just by reading the track alone and the moment i saw the name i was like this is gonna be my favorite song ever and i hope you will enjoy it too um purchase of tracy it's a solo artist from la um she's a 20 year old 21 year old self-tar producer and multi-instrumentalist um so hopefully you have fun with this track a little bit of warning a language warning for you there and after that in the last 30 minutes um we'll have more track from sydney locals yubari and the new sydney phillips album of course um one of our favorites here at the station again you're on tuesday morning text in tell me how feel at 0 4 3 5 1 2 3 9 4 5 and without further ado here is portraits of Tracy"}, {"start": "01:29:57", "end": "01:30:26", "text": "You're listening to Mornings. The Book of Everything is back. Directed by Neil Armfield and based on the novel by Gus Kaya. Follow Thomas who can see the extraordinary as he navigates the changing world around him. A child who learns what to do when he's most afraid and how to face the wrong in the world. Happening August 22 to September 20. Tickets available from Belvoir.com.au. Belvoir Street Theatre. Sponsors of FBi Radio."}, {"start": "01:40:59", "end": "01:42:17", "text": "Such a great mix by Yubari. It's called I Want That, Base Base Base, 135 BPM. Yubari is an independent experimental electronic producer here in Eora, Sydney. And we're going to keep that going here on Tuesday morning with Blair Romance, the second EP, I'm Not the Same, the track I'm going to play. it's called velvet teeth with cherry ripe another one of our local favorites here at fbi and if you want to keep these independent sydney artists discovered support us here at fbi.radio slash support and we have about 20 minutes left stay tuned for more sydney tracks and the show after that wild card with steward you're on tuesday morning with august here at fbi radio 94.5 and a little language warning for you for this track but here is velvet teeth by blair romans cherry ripe and bren"}, {"start": "01:44:43", "end": "01:45:03", "text": "4.5 The best gigs in Sydney. We're there, front of stage, on the live feed. This month, you can catch the recording of Kisses, live at Judith Nielsen's Phoenix Central Park."}, {"start": "01:51:52", "end": "01:52:32", "text": "You just heard Animal by Riki Twinkle Wells. Just jumping in here for the last time. Thank you so much for tuning in. It's the end of Tuesday morning with August. But stay seated for Wild Card with Stewart because we're on air 24-7 here on FBi 94.5. And I'm going to play you the last two tracks from the new Man Woman Chainsaw album. and some boats to canada as always yeah stay tuned thank you so much for tuning in have you are having a lovely day this is fbi radio 94.5"}, {"start": "01:58:36", "end": "01:5